 "final_text": "## CESP four-week cash forecast \u2014 submitted\n\n**Methodology (per TRS-SOP-004, Treasury's standard cash-forecast assumptions):**\n- Direct method, weeks run Monday\u2013Sunday, week 1 = the week containing today (2026-08-11)\n- Receipts = open AR invoices collected in the week of their due date (past-due-at-start invoices excluded)\n- Disbursements = open AP invoices paid in the week of their due date (same exclusion)\n- Payroll = funding dates from the people.ops payroll calendar that fall inside the window\n- Net/week = receipts \u2212 disbursements \u2212 payroll; no opening-balance roll-in\n\n**What I found for CESP (dataareaid `CESP` = \"CES Programs LLC\"):**\n- **AR (CustomerTransactions):** exactly 3 open invoices, all due 2026\u201103\u201105/12/18 \u2014 all already >4 months past due at the 2026\u201108\u201111 forecast start, so excluded per rule 1.\n- **AP (VendorTransactions):** exactly 3 open invoices, due 2026\u201103\u201104/11/25 \u2014 same exclusion, rule 2.\n- **Payroll:** `CESP-payroll-calendar-2026.xlsx` has only 3 funding dates, all Feb/Mar 2026 \u2014 none fall in the Aug 10\u2013Sep 6 window, so excluded per rule 3.\n- Cross-checked completeness: filtered CESP records against the full (5,795-row AR / 5,440-row AP) unfiltered dataset to confirm no CESP rows were missed among the USMF noise; confirmed Docs has exactly one SOP (already read), Books has no customer records for this entity, and Email has nothing relevant.\n\n**Result:** every open AR/AP item and every payroll date on record predates the forecast window, so all four weeks come out flat.\n\n| Week | Net |\n|---|---|\n| Week 1 | $0 |\n| Week 2 | $0 |\n| Week 3 | $0 |\n| Week 4 | $0 |\n| **4-week total** | **$0** |\n\nSubmitted via `submit_answer`. Worth flagging to Robin separately: the payroll calendar file hasn't been updated since Jan 5 2026 (last entry Mar 27) and the only open AR/AP on CESP's books are stale March invoices \u2014 those are probably worth a data-hygiene follow-up before Thursday's board call, independent of this zero-flow answer.",
